     3,
     "<div><blockquote type=\"cite\">\r\n            Hi all, <div><br></div><div>I am trying to run one file in GGIR (reason: because when I ran it with the rest of the dataset it provided no data in part 2 (for steps) but data in part5). However, when running the single files I get the following error: </div><div><br></div><div>&quot;<span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11);font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px\">Error in length(peak_info) == 0 || length(peak_info) == sum(<a href=\"http://is.na\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://is.na&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792489039795000&amp;usg=AOvVaw08gdpKqYixlxJn3kwJj_WH\">is.na</a>(peak_info)) : </span></div><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;line-height:1.2\" role=\"document\" aria-label=\"Console Output\"><span style=\"outline:none\" role=\"document\"><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\">  &#39;length = 5&#39; in coercion to &#39;logical(1)&#39;</span><font color=\"#000000\">&quot;</font></span></span><div><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;line-height:1.2\" role=\"document\" aria-label=\"Console Output\"><span style=\"outline:none\" role=\"document\"><font color=\"#000000\"><br></font></span></span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;line-height:1.2\" role=\"document\" aria-label=\"Console Output\"><span style=\"outline:none\" role=\"document\"><font color=\"#000000\">Full code and output below: </font></span></span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;line-height:1.2\" role=\"document\" aria-label=\"Console Output\"><span style=\"outline:none\" role=\"document\"><font color=\"#000000\"><br></font></span></span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;line-height:1.2\" role=\"document\" aria-label=\"Console Output\"><span style=\"outline:none\" role=\"document\">\r\n\r\n<span style=\"font-size:13.3333px;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;line-height:1.2\" role=\"document\" aria-label=\"Console Output\"><span style=\"outline:none\" role=\"document\"><span style=\"color:blue\">&gt; </span><span style=\"color:blue\">GGIR(#-------------------------------\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             # General parameters\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             #-------------------------------\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             mode=mode,\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             datadir=datadir,\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             outputdir=outputdir,\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             studyname=studyname,\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             f0=f0,\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             f1=f1,\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             overwrite = FALSE,\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             do.imp=TRUE,\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             idloc=1,\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             print.filename=TRUE,\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             storefolderstructure = FALSE,\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             myfun = myfun,\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             #-------------------------------\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             # Part 1 parameters:\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             #-------------------------------\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             windowsizes = c(5,900,3600), #5 s epoch, 15 min non-wear detection resolution, 60 min non-wear evaluation window\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             do.cal=TRUE,\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             do.enmo = TRUE, #ENMO physical activity metric\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             do.anglez=TRUE, # for sleep analysis\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             do.anglex=TRUE,\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             do.angley=TRUE,\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             chunksize=1,\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             acc.metric =&quot;ENMO&quot;,\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             printsummary=TRUE,\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             #-------------------------------\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             # Part 2 parameters:\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             #-------------------------------\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             strategy = 1, #see tutorial for explanation of strategies\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             ndayswindow=7,\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             hrs.del.start = 0,\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             hrs.del.end = 0,\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             maxdur = 9,\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             includedaycrit = 16, # min valid hrs per day\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             qwindow=c(0,24), #window for calculation of quantiles\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             mvpathreshold =c(100,250,400), #thresholds for MVPA, total and bouts 1, 5 &amp; 10 min acceleration&gt;threshold for &gt;80% of time d=or Hildebrand moderate (100) and vigorous thresholds (400) and for brisk walking (250)\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             mvpadur = c(1,5,10),\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             bout.metric = 6,\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             #-------------------------------\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             # Part 3 parameters:\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             #-------------------------------\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             timethreshold= c(5),\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             anglethreshold=5,\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             ignorenonwear = TRUE,\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             #-------------------------------\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             # Part 4 parameters:\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             #-------------------------------\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             excludefirstlast = FALSE,\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             includenightcrit = 16,\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             def.noc.sleep = c(1),\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             #loglocation = sleep_log,\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             outliers.only = FALSE,\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             criterror = 4,\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             relyonsleeplog = FALSE,\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             sleeplogidnum = FALSE,\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             colid=1,\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             coln1=2,\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             do.visual = TRUE,\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             nnights = 8,\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             #-------------------------------\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             # Part 5 parameters:\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             #-------------------------------\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             # Key functions: Merging physical activity with sleep analyses\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             threshold.lig = c(40),\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             threshold.mod = c(100),\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             threshold.vig = c(400),\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             boutcriter = 0.8,\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             <a href=\"http://boutcriter.in\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://boutcriter.in&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792489039795000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2fCLGsJF8tdQsvT2wxl0fL\">boutcriter.in</a> = 0.9,\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             boutcriter.lig = 0.8,\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             boutcriter.mvpa = 0.8,\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             <a href=\"http://boutdur.in\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://boutdur.in&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792489039795000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1s7DWylTaQt2Z74aBsXUhf\">boutdur.in</a> = c(10,20,30),\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             boutdur.lig = c(1,2,5,10),\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             boutdur.mvpa = c(1,2,5,10),\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             timewindow = c(&quot;MM&quot;,&quot;WW&quot;),\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             frag.metrics=&quot;all&quot;, # New frag metrics to inspect\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             part5_agg2_60seconds=TRUE, # Dependency for frag.metrics\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             #-----------------------------------\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             # Report generation\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             #-------------------------------\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             do.report=c(2,3,4,5),\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             visualreport=TRUE,\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             dofirstpage = TRUE,\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             viewingwindow=1)\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px\">\r\nChecking that user has write access permission for directory specified by argument outputdir: Yes\r\n\r\n   GGIR version: 3.1.2\r\n\r\n   Do not forget to cite GGIR in your publications via a version number and\r\n   Migueles et al. 2019 JMPB. doi: 10.1123/jmpb.2018-0063.\r\n   See also: <a href=\"https://cran.r-project.org/package=GGIR/vignettes/GGIR.html#citing-ggir\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://cran.r-project.org/package%3DGGIR/vignettes/GGIR.html%23citing-ggir&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792489039795000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1w-OSFNb6xJNkawJRPOGiB\">https://cran.r-project.org/package=GGIR/vignettes/GGIR.html#citing-ggir</a>\r\n\r\n   To make your research reproducible and interpretable always report:\r\n     (1) Accelerometer brand and product name\r\n     (2) How you configured the accelerometer\r\n     (3) Study protocol and wear instructions given to the participants\r\n     (4) GGIR version\r\n     (5) How GGIR was used: Share the config.csv file or your R script.\r\n     (6) How you post-processed / cleaned GGIR output